$DATUM 2,5-Bis(3-decylthiophen-5-yl)-3,4-dinitrothiophene (S4). S1 (2.48 g, 7.47
mmol), S3 (18.09 mmol), (Ph3P)2PdCl2 (253 mg, 0.36 mmol) and CuI (194 mg,
1.02 mmol) were dissolved in anhydrous 1,4-dioxane (125 mL) under argon
and refluxed overnight. The solvent was evaporated in vacuum and a crude
product was purified by column chromatography on silica gel in
hexane/ethyl acetate (10:1 by vol.). The crude product was recrystallized
by ethanol to give product. Yellow solid, (4.11 g, 89%). 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3): δH (ppm) = 0.89 (t, J = 6.59 Hz, 6H), 1.20-1.42 (m, 28H),
1.57-1.72 (m, 4H), 2.63 (t, J = 7.61 Hz, 4H), 7.16-7.23 (m, 2H) 7.37 (d,
J = 1.46 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δC (ppm) = 144.94, 135.57,
133.93, 132.24, 127.78, 125.98, 31.87, 30.32, 30.27, 29.57, 29.54, 29.37,
29.29, 29.19, 22.66, 14.08.
