$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General coupling procedure A mixture of 1(impure) (0.6mmol), appropriate
heterocyclic bromides (0.5 mmol) and PdCl2(PPh3)2 (0.025mmol) in 10ml dry
DMF was stirred at 120-130 °C for the time given in the Table 1, then
2-5g acid alumina was added in one portion and continue to stir for one
to three hours. After filtering off the alumina, the saturated solution
of ammonium chloride was added in it. The mixture was extracted with
ether or methene dichloride, washed with saturated KF aqueous solution,
dried over MgSO4. After the solvent was removed, the residue was
separated on a chromatography colum with silica gel(eluant:
petroleum/ether), and gave desired products 4. 4f, yield 89%. M.p. °C
150.
