$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of 2-Aryltellurophenes by Stille
Coupling; Typical Procedure 2-(4-Cyanophenyl)tellurophene (3a) To a 25 mL
round-bottom flask was added 4-iodobenzonitrile (0.192 g, 0.84 mmol),
Pd(PPh3)4 (0.048 g, 42 mmol), CsF (0.255 g, 1.68 mmol), CuI (0.016 g, 84
mmol), and then DMF (2 mL). After purging with nitrogen, tellurophene 1
(0.436 g, 0.93 mmol) was added and the mixture was heated at 50-60 °C
overnight. After this time, TLC (hexanes-EtOAc, 3:1) showed the
disappearance of 4- iodobenzonitrile. The reaction was then extracted
with CH2Cl2 and washed with H2O (3 × 10 mL). The extract was dried over
Na2SO4 and concentrated on a rotary evaporator. The yellow solid was then
recrystallized from hexanes (30 mL) to give the product 3a.
2-(4-Nitrophenyl)tellurophene (3d), yellow-orange crystals, yield 0.220
g, 88%. mp 102 °C (hexanes). IR: 3097, 3071, 1584, 1522, 1500, 1430,
1370, 1317, 1260, 1207, 1184, 1113, 850, 828, 749, 686, 679 cm-1. 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 9.02 (dd, J = 1.2, 6.8 Hz, 1 H), 8.20 (d, J = 8.8
Hz, 2 H), 7.98 (dd, J = 1.2, 4.1 Hz, 1 H), 7.88 (dd, J = 4.0, 6.5 Hz, 1
H), 7.60 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 147.2, 146.9,
139.5, 136.6, 132.1, 130.0, 127.8, 124.9. Anal. Calcd for C10H7NO2Te: C,
39.93; H, 2.35; N, 4.66. Found: C, 40.00; H, 2.24; N, 4.61.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Stille cross-coupling reactions of 2-(tributylstannyl)- and
2,5-bis(trimethylstannyl)tellurophene
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sweat, Daniel P.; Stephens, Chad E.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2009), (19), 3214-3218

