$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method A: A mixture of
3,5-dibromo-1-methyl-1H-1,2,4-triazole (1) (200 mg, 0.83 mmol), stannyl
derivative (2) (1.08 mmol), PdCl2(PPh3)2 (12 mg, 0.017 mmol) and LiCl
(106 mg, 2.49 mmol) or CuI (15.8 mg, 0.083 mmol) was irradiated under
Argon in a focused microwave reactor DiscoverTM (CEM) at 110 °C for 15
min. The crude products 3a and 4a-g were purified by flash chromatography
on silica gel using a mixture of hexane:ethyl acetate as the eluent.
3-Bromo-1-methyl-5-(1-methyl-1H-pyrrol-2-yl)-1H-1,2,4-triazole 4b :Method
A. 1-methyl-2- (tributylstannyl)-1H-pyrrole 2b (399 mg, 1.08 mmol) and
LiCl were used. The crude was purified with a mixture of hexane:ethyl
acetate (6:1) as the eluent, 4b (176 mg, 88%) was obtained. Mp 41-42 °C;
1H NMR (CDCl3): δ = 6.74 (t, J = 1.8 Hz, 1 H, H-5''), 6.41 (dd, J = 4.0,
1.5 Hz, 1 H, H-3''), 6.14 (dd, J = 3.7, 2.6 Hz, 1 H, H-4''), 4.06 (s, 3
H, CH3); 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ = 149.9, 138.3, 126.8, 118.3, 113.1, 108.2,
37.1 (CH3), 36.0 (CH3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Stille reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microwave-assisted Stille reactions as a powerful tool for building
polyheteroaryl systems bearing a (1H)-1,2,4-triazole moiety
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
