$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-(tert-Butoxycarbonyl)-2-(4,5-dimethoxy-2-vinylphenyl)ethylamine: To a
solution of 0.0322 g (0.0791 mmol, 1.0 eq.) of iodide 6a in 4 mL abs DMF
were added 0.0083 g (0.0316 mmol, 0.4 eq.) AsPh3 and the mixture was
degassed for 5 minutes by bubbling Argon through the mixture. Then 0.0123
g (0.0134 mmol, 0.17eq.) of the Pd catalyst were added followed by 0.058
mL (0.1977 mmol, 2.5 eq.) of the stannane. The mixture was stirred at
room temperature for 3 days, filtered through a HPLC filter, washed with
water (4 × 10 mL) and brine, dried over MgSO4, filtered, and the solvent
was removed under reduced pressure. The crude product was purified by
flash chromatography on silica (eluent: hexane/ethyl acetate 3:1) of 12.
Colorless crystals, yield 0.0214 g, 0.0694 mmol, 88%. Rf (hexane/ethyl
acetate 3:1) 0.28. M.p.: 122-123 °C. IR (film): 3378, 2975, 2934, 1694,
1605, 1509, 1463, 1365, 1263, 1219, 1166, 1102, 1053, 989, 862. 1H-NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.01 (s, 1H, 3-Harom.), 6.90 (dd, J = 7.3, 10.9, 1H,
CH=CH2), 6.62 (s, 1H, 6-Harom.), 5.54 (dd, J = 7.3, J = .0, 1H,
CH=CHcisHtrans), 5.21 (dd, J = 0.9, J = .1, 1H, CH=CHcisHtrans), 4.60
(bs, 1H, NH), 3.88, (s, 3H, OCH3), 3.85 (s, 3H, OCH3), 3.27 (d, J = .32,
2H, CH2N), 2.81 (t, J = .11, 2H, ArCH2), 1.42 (s, 9H, C(CH3)3). 13C-NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 155.96, 148.91, 147.86, 13384, 129.19, 129.13,
113.90, 112.99, 108.63, 79.21, 55.99, 41.67, 33.08, 28.50. ESI: 330.2 ([M
+ Na]+, C17H25NO4Na, calcd. 330.4. HRMS: 330.1675 ([M + Na]+);
C17H25NNaO4, calcd. 330.1676.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A ring-closing metathesis-based approach to the synthesis of
(+)-tetrabenazine
