$DATUM 2-(4-methoxypyridin-2-yl)-4-(trifluoromethyl)quinoline (16d): To an oven
dried 25 mL round bottomed flask with a stirbar was weighed the aryl
bromide 10 (134.2 mg, 0.486 mmol, 1.07 equiv.), Pd(Ph3P)2Cl2 (16.1 mg,
0.023 mmol, 0.05 equiv.), and Ph3P (12.3 mg, 0.047 mmol, 0.10 equiv.).
Dry toluene was charged to the flask and the solution was sparged with N2
for 20 min. The pyridyl stannane 17d (186.1 mg, 0.47 mmol, 1 equiv.) was
added to the flask via syringe addition. A water cooled condenser was
attached to the flask and the reaction mixture was heated to reflux
overnight. After 16 h, the reaction was cooled to room temperature and
transferred to a separatory funnel with CH2Cl2 (20 mL). The organic
mixture was washed with saturated NaHCO3 (1 × 30 mL) solution, which was
subsequently back extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 × 20 mL). The combined
organics were dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo.
Purified by flash chromatography eluting with hexanes containing 20%
ethyl acetate and 2% triethyl amine to provide the product 16d as a light
yellow solid (126.4 mg, 0.415 mmol) in 88% yield. Rf = 0.36 (20% Ethyl
Acetate, 2.5 % Triethylamine in hexanes), UV M.P.: 112-114 °C 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ 4.03 (s, 3H), 6.95 (m, 1H), 7.70 (dd, J= 8.2, 8.2 Hz, 1H),
7.85 (dd, J= 7.4, 8.2 Hz, 1H), 8.19 (d, J= 8.6 Hz, 1H), 8.25 (dd, J= 2.3,
2.3 Hz, 1H), 8.30 (d, J= 8.6 Hz, 1H), 8.58 (dd, J= 2.0, 5.5 Hz, 1H), 8.94
(s, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 55.6, 107.0, 111.8, 116.7 (q, J= 4.6
Hz), 123.7 (q, J= 101 Hz), 124.2, 128.5, 130.4, 130.9, 135.1 (q, J= 32
Hz), 148.8, 150.6, 155.8, 157.1, 166.9. IR (neat): 3099 (w), 2970 (w),
1601 (s), 1353 (m) cm-1 HRMS: m/z (ESI/TOF MS E+) Calculated[MH+]
305.0896, observed 305.0887.
