$DATUM 2-Bromo-3-dodecyl-5-vinylthiophene, 5 (Stille Coupling).
2-Bromo-3-dodecyl-5-iodothiophene (6.25 g, 13.7 mmol) was dissolved in 60
mL of toluene. The solution was sparged of oxygen by bubbling nitrogen
through the system for 20 min. Pd2(dba)3 (313 mg, 2.5 mol %) and Ph3P
(360 mg, 10 mol %) are then added. The system is placed in a 60 °C oil
bath and tributyl(vinyl)tin was then added (4.16 mL, 14.2 mmol). The
solution was stirred for 6 h. The system was cooled and then filtered
through a silica plug (using toluene as eleunt). The filtrate was washed
with water (100 mL). The aqueous layer was washed twice (2 • 25 mL) with
ethyl ether, and the organic layers were dried over sodium sulfate.
Filtration and rotary evaporation afforded the crude product in 88%
yield. Crystallization at -40 °C in pentane. Pure product (2.85 g) in 58%
yield. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 6.87 (d, 1H), 6.64 (s, 1H), 6.59 (d, 1H), 5.32
(d, 1H), 5.09 (d, 1H), 2.48 (t, 2H), 1.54 (m, 2H), 1.25 (m, 18H), 0.87
(t, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 142.4, 142.3, 129.6, 126.8, 118.1, 113.2,
31.90, 29.67, 29.60, 29.58, 29.48, 29.43, 29.38, 29.20, 22.70, 14.11.
Anal. Calcd for C18H29BrS: C = 60.49, H = 8.18, Br = 22.36. Found: C =
60.45, H = 8.33, Br = 22.20.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille coupling, alternative preparation shown
