$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 123-91-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure For the Synthesis of
Sterically Hindered Biaryls Using Ligand 3 (Procedure C). In a glove box,
the Schlenk tube equipped with a stir bar was charged with Pd2(dba)3 (7
mg, 0.0075 mmol, 1.5 mol %), CsF (168 mg, 1.1 mmol), and ligand 3 (7.2
mg, 0.0175 mmol, 3.5 mol %). The tube was fitted with a rubber septum and
removed out of the glove box. Aryl halide (1.0 equiv), 1,4-dioxane (1
mL), and organotin reagent (1.1 equiv) were added successively using
syringes. The tube was sealed with a Teflon screwcap. The reaction
mixture was stirred for 30 minutes at room temperature then heated with
stirring at the indicated temperature for the indicated time. The
reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, diluted with ether or
acetone, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel.
2,4,6,2’,5’-Pentamethylbiphenyl (Table 5, entry 2). Procedure C was
followed using 2-chloro-p-xylene (71 mg, 0.5 mmol) and
2-mesityltributylstannane (225 mg, 0.55 mmol). After the reaction was run
for 48 h, the reaction mixture was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel (hexanes) to afford 98 mg (88%) of the desired product as a
colorless liquid. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.18 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H),
7.07 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 6.95 (s, 2H), 6.85 (s, 1H), 2.35 (s, 6H), 1.94
(s, 9H). 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3): δ 140.6, 138.6, 136.4, 135.9, 132.8,
129.9, 128.2, 127.8, 21.3, 21.3, 20.5, 19.2. HRMS m/z Calcd for C17H20:
224.15650. Found 224.15692.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly active palladium catalysts supported by bulky proazaphosphatrane
ligands for Stille cross-coupling: Coupling of aryl and vinyl chlorides,
