$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Entry 1 A mixture of POPd (16.0 mg, 6 mol %),
ary lhalide derivative (0.6 mmol), phenyltrimethylstannane (0.7 mmol),
and Cy2NMe (120 mg, 0.61 mmol) was stirred in 5 mL of deionized water at
140 °C using a closed vessel. After 24 h, the reaction mixture was
allowed to cool to room temperature and extracted with Et2O. The combined
organic layers were washed with brine and dried over MgSO4, and the
solvents were removed under vacuum. 4-Phenylquinoline, 5.17 Purification
by chromatography on silica gel using hexanes/ethyl
acetate/triethylamine, 100:10:1. 1H NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.34 (d, J =
4.4 Hz, 1H), 7.50-7.52 (m, 6H), 7.73 (dd, J = 7.0 Hz, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H),
7.92 (d, J =7.0 Hz, 1H), 8.18 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 8.95 (d, J = 4.4 Hz,
1H).13C NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 121.5, 126.1, 126.8, 128.6, 128.8,129.5,
129.7, 130.0, 138.2, 148.7, 148.8, 150.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry (recyclable catalyst), green chemistry-solvent, Still
cross-coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Stille Cross-Coupling Reaction Using Aryl Chlorides or Bromides
in Water
