$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(4-(tert-butyl)pyridin-2-yl)-4-(trifluoromethyl)quinoline (16c): To an
oven dried 25 mL round bottomed flask with a stirbar was weighed the aryl
bromide 10 (1348 mg, 0.50 mmol, 1.07 equiv.), Pd(Ph3P)2Cl2 (16.1 mg,
0.023 mmol, 0.05 equiv.), and Ph3P (12.3 mg, 0.047 mmol, 0.10 equiv.).
Dry toluene was charged to the flask and the solution was sparged with N2
for 20 min. The pyridyl stannane 17c (199.5 mg, 0.47 mmol, 1 equiv.) was
charged to the flask by syringe. A water cooled condenser was attached to
the flask and the reaction mixture was heated to reflux overnight. After
16 h, the reaction was cooled to room temperature and transferred to a
separatory funnel with CH2Cl2 (20 mL). The organic mixture was washed
with saturated NaHCO3 (1 × 30 mL) solution, which was subsequently back
extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 × 20 mL). The combined organics were dried over
Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. Purified by flash
chromatography eluting with hexanes containing 5% ethyl acetate and 1%
triethyl amine to provide the product 16c as a slightly yellow solid
(137.0 mg, 0.415 mmol) in 88% yield. Rf = 0.31 (10% ethyl acetate, 1%
triethyl amine in hexanes) UV M.P.: 64-66 °C, 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ
1.45 (s, 9H), 7.41 (dd, J= 1.9, 5.2 Hz, 1H), 7.68 (ddd, J= 1.1, 6.9, 8.2
Hz, 1H), 7.83 (ddd, J= 1.4, 6.9, 8.5 Hz, 1H), 8.18 (d, J= 8.5 Hz, 1H),
8.32 (d, J= 8.5 Hz, 1H), 8.67 (d, J= 5.2 Hz, 1H), 8.70 (d, J= 1.4 Hz,
1H), 8.95 (s, 1H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 30.8, 35.3, 116.8 (q, J=
5.8 Hz), 118.8, 122.1, 124.1, 124.2, 124.4 (q, J= 205 Hz) 128.4, 130.3,
130.9, 134.6 (q, J= 32 Hz), 148.8, 149.4, 155.1, 156.3, 161.5 IR (neat):
3095 (w), 3064 (w), 2699 (m), 2906 (w), 2871 (w), 1610 (m), 1598 (s),
1335 (s) cm-1. HRMS: m/z (ESI/TOF MS E+) Calculated[MH+] 331.1417,
observed 331.1416.
