$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Stille Couplings; General Procedure 1: An
oven-dried Schlenk tube was charged with LiCl (2.0 equiv) and heated with
a heat gun under vacuum (< 0.1 mbar). After cooling to room temperature,
CuI (2.0 equiv), (substituted) o-iodoaniline (1.0 equiv) and Pd(PPh3)4 (5
mol%) were added and the flask was evacuated and refilled with Ar three
times. DMF (10 mL/mmol), which was previously degassed by bubbling with
Ar, and the organotin compound (1.2 equiv) were added and the mixture was
heated to 80 °C for 18 h. Upon reaching full conversion (TLC analysis),
the mixture was diluted with EtOAc and 1 M KF solution (5 mL/mmol) was
added. Upon vigorous shaking (in the Schlenk tube) a colourless
precipitate formed and the mixture was filtered through a pad of Celite
with EtOAc. The layers were separated and the aqueous layer was extracted
twice with EtOAc. The combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4,
filtered and concentrated. The residue was purified by (automated) flash
chromatography. tert-Butyl
N-Trifluoroacetyl-2-amino-4-(2-amino-phenyl)pent-4-enoate (3a) According
to general procedure 1 55.9 mg (0.250 mmol) of 2-iodoaniline were reacted
with 1 (172 mg, 0.300 mmol), LiCl (21 mg, 0.500 mmol), CuI (95 mg, 0.500
mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4 (14 mg, 12.5 µmol). Automated flash chromatography
(PE/EtOAc 100:0, 80:20). tert-Butyl
N-Trifluoroacetyl-2-amino-4-(2-amino-5-chloro-phenyl)pent-4-enoate (3b)
According to general procedure 1 127 mg (0.500 mmol) of
4-chloro-2-iodoaniline were reacted with 1 (371 mg, 0.600 mmol), LiCl (42
mg, 1.00 mmol), CuI (190 mg, 1.00 mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4 (29 mg, 25 µmol.
Flash chromatography (PE/EtOAc 80:20). 170 mg (0.433 mmol, 87%) of 3b as
a brown solid. mp: 104-105 °C. Rf = 0.22 (PE/EtOAc 80:20). 1H-NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.42 (s, 9 H, 6-H), 2.93 (dd, J = 14.2, 5.0 Hz, 1 H,
7-Ha), 3.06 (ddd, J = 14.2, 5.4, 0.5 Hz, 1 H, 7-Hb), 3.82 (bs, 2 H, NH2),
4.58 (m, 1 H, 3-H), 5.23 (d, J = 1.4 Hz, 1 H, 9-Ha), 5.47 (m, 1 H, 9-Hb),
6.29 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1 H, 12-H), 6.95 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1 H, 15-H), 7.03
(dd, J = 8.5, 2.4 Hz, 1 H, 13-H), 7.35 (d, J = 6.7 Hz, 1 H, TFAN-H).
13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 27.9 (C-6), 38.7 (C-7), 52.4 (C-3), 83.5
(C-5), 117.5 (C-12), 120.4 (C-9), 123.5 (C-14, only observable in
HMBC),128.3, 128.4, 128.4 (C-10, C-13, C-15), 141.1, 141.1 (C-8, C-11),
156.4 (q, 2JC2,F = 37.9 Hz, C-2), 168.9 (C-4). The signal of C-1 could
not be observed. HRMS (CI) C17H20F3N2O3Cl [M]+; calculated 392.1109;
found 392.1115.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, Stille coupling, Schlenk tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Straightforward Protocol for the Synthesis of Functionalized Tryptophan
Peptides via Stille Coupling, Azidation and Photoinduced Nitrene
Insertion
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Junk, Lukas; Kazmaier, Uli
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
