$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Stille Coupling:
Preparation of Trifluoromethanesulfonic Acid
2-[Benzyl-(4-methoxy-2-phenylbut-2-enoyl)-amino]phenyl Ester (10). A
stirred mixture of Pd2dba3·CHCl3 (6 mg, 0.006 mmol), P(2-furyl)3 (12 mg,
0.051 mmol), and freshly distilled N-methylpyyrolidinone (NMP, 2 mL) was
deoxygenated by bubbling Ar through a submerged needle for 1 h, during
which time a bright yellow solution resulted. A deoxygenated solution of
stannane 9 (200 mg, 0.28 mmol), iodobenzene (52 mg, 0.25 mmol), and NMP
(5 mL) was then added via syringe. Copper(I) iodide (46 mg, 0.28 mmol)
was then added, and the resulting mixture was flushed with a stream of Ar
for 15 min and then maintained at room temperature for 24 h. After
diluting the reaction with EtOAc (100 mL), the resulting solution was
washed with 5% aqueous NH4OH (3 × 10 mL) and brine (3 × 10 mL). The
organic layer was dried (Na2SO4) and filtered, and the filtrate was
concentrated. The residue was purified by flash chromatography (1:9-3:7
EtOAc-hexanes). Trifluoromethanesulfonic acid
2-{benzyl-[2-(2-tert-butoxycarbonylaminophenyl)-4-methoxy-but-2-enoyl]-amino}phenyl
ester (11i). The general procedure for the Stille coupling was followed
using stannane 9 (6.0 g, 8.34 mmol), N-Boc-2-iodoaniline (2.93 g, 9.17
mmol), Pd(dba)2 (478 mg, 830 μmol, 10 mol%), P(2-furyl)3 (871 mg, 3.75
mmol, 0.6 eq.), and CuI (1.75 g, 9.17 mmol) in NMP (47 mL). Silica gel
chromatography (hexanes-ether, 10:1-3:1, v/v) of the crude residue gave
11i (4.5 g, 87% yield, 14:1 mixture of amide rotamers) as a yellow oil.
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, major rotamer) δ 7.99 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H),
7.32-7.23 (m, 6H), 7.19 (dd, J = 7.4, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 7.09 (dt, J = 6.9, 1.2
Hz, 1H), 7.04 (s, 1H), 6.88 (dt, J = 6.3, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 6.61 (dt, J = 6.0,
1.0 Hz, 1H), 6.33 (dd, J = 6.4, 1.1 Hz, 1H), 6.20 (dd, J = 6.1, 1.0 Hz,
1H), 5.81 (t, J = 4.9 Hz, 1H), 5.78 (d, J = 11.5 Hz, 1H), 4.28 (dq, J =
19.4, 4.9 Hz, 2H), 4.07 (d, J = 12.3 Hz, 1H), 3.39 (s, 1H), (s, 9H); 13C
NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 168.7, 152.5, 145.4, 136.0, 136.5, 136.2, 135.9,
132.9, 132.1, 129.8, 129.1, 128.5, 128.5, 128.3, 128.1, 127.8, 126.9,
122.4, 121.3, 119.0, 118.1 (J CF = 319 Hz), 80.1, 69.6, 58.3, 52.3, 28.2;
IR (thin film) 1733, 1648, 1586, 1525, 1393, 1220, 1154, 891, 768 cm-1;
HRMS (EI) calcd for C30H31F3N2O7SNa: 643.1702; found: 643.1697. Anal.
Calcd for C30H31F3N2O7S: C, 58.06; H, 5.03; N, 4.51. Found: C, 57.11; H,
4.96; N, 4.32.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM anaerobic, stereoselective, Stille coupling reaction, 14:1 mixt. of amide
rotamers
