$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5,5'-Diphenyl-[2,4']bisoxazole 8 A 5 mL microwave vial was charged with
4-iodo-5-phenyloxazole3 (100 mg, 0.37 mmol, 1 equiv),
5-phenyl-2-tributylstannanyl-oxazole 4a (481 mg, 1.11 mmol, 3 equiv),
Pd2(dba)3 (17 mg, 5 mol %), PCy3 (10 mg, 10 mol %), and anhydrous DMF (5
mL). The microwave vial was then sealed, and the resulting mixture
stirred at rt for 5 min prior to irradiation at a pre-selected
temperature of 150°C in a Smith Synthesizer for 5 min. The vial was then
cooled with air jet cooling, opened and poured into a mixture of
saturated aqueous KF (20 mL) and EtOAc (20 mL) and stirred for 30 min.
After this time the organic layer was separated and the aqueous layer
extracted twice with EtOAc. The organic layers were combined, dried over
Mg2SO4 and filtered through celite. The solvent was removed in vacuo and
the residue purified by flash column chromatography (silica doped with
10% KF, hexane/Et2O 6:4) to give the coupled product 8 (56 mg, 87% yield)
as a white solid. 5,5'-Diphenyl-[2,4']bisoxazole 8, yield 56 mg, 87% Mp =
102-104°C. 1H NMR (360 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.42-7.54 (7H, m), 7.74-7.76 (m,
2H), 8.04 (1H, s), 8.29-8.31 (2H, m). 13C NMR (90 MHz, CDCl3) δ 123.1
(CH), 124.2 (CH), 126.9 (quat), 127.3 (CH), 127.4 (quat), 128.4 (CH),
128.5 (CH), 128.7 (CH), 128.8 (quat), 129.8 (CH), 149.7 (CH), 150.0
(quat), 151.3 (quat), 154.9 (quat). HRMS (ESI) calculated for C18H12N2O2
289.0972 found 289.0974.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, sealed tube used, yield depends on reaction
conditions (time, temp, base, cat.,and additive)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Regioselective Palladium Cross-Coupling of 2,4-Dihalooxazoles: Convergent
Synthesis of Trisoxazoles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Flegeau, Emmanuel Ferrer; Popkin, Matthew E.; Greaney, Michael F.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2008), 73(8), 3303-3306

