$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative Procedure for N-Benzyl, N-(2-Styryl)-tosylamide 3. A
flame-dried Schlenk tube was charged with CuCl (128 mg, 1.3 mmol) and
AsPh3 (9 mg, 0.03 mmol), and the mixture was degassed three times under
vacuum with a dry nitrogen purge. Anhydrous THF (10 mL) was introduced
with concomitant stirring, and the resulting mixture was again degassed
twice by the freeze-thaw process. Pd2dba3 (12 mg, 0.012 mmol) was then
introduced, and the mixture was degassed once. When the solution was
warmed to room temperature (30 min), PhI (31 μL, 0.27 mmol) was added;
the mixture turned brownish, and the resulting suspension was stirred for
30 min before adding 2 (139 mg, 0.24 mmol). After being stirred at room
temperature for an additional hour, the mixture was heated to 60 °C and
the reaction completion was monitored by TLC. The reaction mixture was
cooled, filtered over a plug of Celite (1 cm), and rinsed five times with
10 mL of ether, × and the solution was concentrated to a residue that was
purified by flash chromatography over silica gel and recrystallized from
pentane/ether. 77 mg (87% yield) of 3 as colorless crystals. Rf : 0.32
(80:20 pentane/EtOAc). 1H NMR (300.13 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.76 (bd, J = 8.5
Hz, 2H), 7.3-7.15 (m, 12H), 5.45 (s, 1H), 5.03 (s, 1H), 4.57 (s, 2H),
2.44 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (75.47 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 21.72, 53.19, 114.63, 126.89,
127.86, 128.05, 128.44, 128.73, 129.18, 129.67, 136.24, 136.72, 137.21,
143.71, 145.03. MS (CI/NH3) m/z: 364 (M + 1, 100), 381 (M + 18, 24).
HR-MS (EI) m/z: calcd for C22H21NO2S [M+], 363.1293; found, 363.1296.
FTIR (KBr) ν: 1621, 1599, 1493, 1455, 1351, 1164. Mp: 100.3-100.4 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
